I see exactly what happened here.
 1. **Why special characters still appeared in Branch/CGL:** In Material UI (MUI), an <Autocomplete> manages its own internal text unless you explicitly tell it to use your state by adding the inputValue prop. Because that prop was missing, it fired the warning, cleaned the state, but *visually* allowed the character to stay in the box.
 2. **Why CGL search broke:** You accidentally pasted the onChange logic meant for the **Amount** field into the **CGL** dropdown! That completely broke the dropdown's ability to select a CGL item.
 3. **Amount field warning:** The logic for the Amount field didn't get updated in the last copy-paste.
Let's fix all of this right now. Here are the precise replacements to make your form perfectly strict.
### 1. Fix the Branch Autocomplete (Strict Input)
Find the <Autocomplete> component for **Branch** (around line 527). We are going to add the inputValue prop to control the text, and clean up the onInputChange.
**Find this block:**
```javascript
                    value={row.branch}
                    onChange={(event, newValue) =>
                      handleRowChange(row.id, "branch", newValue)
                    }
                  onInputChange={(event, newInputValue) => {
                      if (event && event.type === 'change') {
                        // User typed something -> filter & warn
                        const cleanInput = filterAndWarn(newInputValue, "alphanumeric_space");
                        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: cleanInput }));
                        searchBranches(cleanInput, row.id);
                      } else {
                        // Dropdown selection occurred
                        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: newInputValue }));
                      }
                    }}
                    loading={branchSearch.loadingId === row.id}

```
**Replace with:**
```javascript
                    value={row.branch}
                    onChange={(event, newValue) =>
                      handleRowChange(row.id, "branch", newValue)
                    }
                    // This forces the input box to strictly show ONLY the filtered value
                    inputValue={branchInputValues[row.id] || ""}
                    onInputChange={(event, newInputValue, reason) => {
                      if (reason === 'input') {
                        const cleanInput = filterAndWarn(newInputValue, "alphanumeric_space");
                        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: cleanInput }));
                        searchBranches(cleanInput, row.id);
                      } else {
                        setBranchInputValues(prev => ({ ...prev, [row.id]: newInputValue }));
                      }
                    }}
                    loading={branchSearch.loadingId === row.id}

```
