### 3. Fix the Amount Field (Add Snackbar Warning)
Find the <TextField> for **Amount** (around line 720).
**Find this block:**
```javascript
                    onChange={(e) => {
                      const val = e.target.value;
                      // Dynamic strict validation based on selected currency
                      if (val === "" || amountRegex.test(val)) {
                        handleRowChange(row.id, "amount", val);
                      }
                    }}

```
**Replace with:**
```javascript
                    onChange={(e) => {
                      const rawVal = e.target.value;
                      
                      // 1. Check for totally illegal characters instantly
                      if (/[^0-9.]/.test(rawVal)) {
                        showSnackBar("Only numbers and decimal point are allowed.", "warning");
                        return; // Block the character
                      }

                      // 2. Enforce the strict digit/decimal limits
                      if (rawVal === "" || amountRegex.test(rawVal)) {
                        handleRowChange(row.id, "amount", rawVal);
                      } else {
                        showSnackBar("Exceeded maximum digits or decimal places.", "warning");
                      }
                    }}

```
By adding inputValue={...} to your Autocompletes, React will actively block the special characters from rendering on the screen the moment filterAndWarn strips them out! Your CGL selection will also start working perfectly again.
